ge, done. If I had two more features to build, I could spin up two more worktrees and have them all running simultaneously.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 9. Queued Messages \u2014 SLIDE + DEMO (2\u20133 min)\n\n### Slide talk track:\n> *\"Queued Messages let you send your next prompt while Cascade is still working. If you already know what you want, queue it up. It also makes managing multiple conversations much easier.\"*\n\n### Prompt 5 + Prompt 6 (queued)\n> **Mode:** Code\n\nSend the first prompt:\n```\nAdd a \"last updated\" timestamp at the bottom of the Unsigned Notes panel on the dashboard that shows \"Last checked:\" followed by the current time\n```\n\n**Immediately** type and queue the second:\n```\nAdd the same \"last updated\" timestamp to the Pending Orders panel\n```\n\n**Talk track:**\n> *\"I just queued two prompts \u2014 the second one is waiting. No downtime, no context switching. Cascade handles them back-to-back. This is huge when you're in flow and know exactly what needs to happen.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 10. Adaptive Mode \u2014 SLIDE (2 min)\n\n> *\"Adaptive Mode is a new model mode that routes Cascade to the optimal model for every task. It determines the correct model from our list, works with enterprise model configurations, enables adaptive credit usage, and lets you see which model was used in the response statistics.\"*\n\n> *\"What this enables: you stop thinking about which model to pick. Simple CSS change? Fast model. Complex refactor? Frontier model. Adaptive handles it.\"*\n\n**Show the model selector in Windsurf, switch to Adaptive.**\n\n---\n\n## 11. Agent Command Center \u2014 SLIDE (1\u20132 min)\n\n> *\"The Agent Command Center is a new command center to manage all agents running on the Cognition Platform. You get a kanban interface for active, blocked, and ready-for-review agents. It's tailored to agent-first development.\"*\n\n> *\"What this enables: developing and merging code faster while maintaining clear oversight. You can have multiple agents working in parallel \u2014 one on the frontend, one on the backend, one writing tests \u2014 and manage them all from one place.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 12. Spaces \u2014 SLIDE (1\u20132 min)\n\n> *\"Spaces organize all work done across multiple agents. All sessions within a space share context \u2014 so if one agent learns something about the codebase, the others benefit.\"*\n\n> *\"New sessions automatically share context, you can easily switch between tasks, and you can use different types of agents within a space. This enables true cross-agent collaboration and better organization.\"*\n\n---\n\n## 13. Support \u2014 SLIDE (1 min)\n\n> *\"Windsurf has a dedicated support engineering team in the USA and India. Enterprise customers are prioritized by default \u2014 you must be logged in when filing a ticket.\"*\n\n> *\"If you encounter bugs: first, file a support ticket at windsurf.com/support and include your diagnostics log. Post in the Slack channel only after filing a ticket with the support team.\"*\n\n---\n\n## Closing (1\u20132 min)\n\n> *\"Let me recap what we covered:*\n> 1. **Purpose Built Models** \u2014 preference data advantage, SWE 1.5 at 13\u00d7 speed\n> 2. **Fast Context** \u2014 SWE-grep, 20\u00d7 faster retrieval, noise-free\n> 3. **DeepWiki** \u2014 instant knowledge, onboarding, code \u2194 docs bridge\n> 4. **Deep Codebase Understanding** \u2014 4\u00d7 more accurate retrieval\n> 5. **Codemaps** \u2014 visual code intelligence, shareable, AI-ready\n> 6. **Hooks & Skills** \u2014 logging, security, guidance, reusable knowledge\n> 7. **Git Worktrees** \u2014 parallel agentic development\n> 8. **Queued Messages** \u2014 no downtime between prompts\n> 9. **Adaptive Mode** \u2014 automatic model routing\n> 10. **Agent Command Center & Spaces** \u2014 manage agents at scale\n>\n> *If you have questions, now's the time.\"*\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference: All Prompts\n\n| # | Prompt | Feature Demonstrated |\n|---|--------|---------------------|\n| 1 | `Give 