    "response": "*Rules used for this response:*\n- (Always On) Triggered Rule: AGENTS.md\n\n### Planner Response\n\nI\u2019ll inspect the repository structure and key README/source entry points to summarize what this codebase does at a high level.\n\n*Found code context*\n\n### Planner Response\n\nI found the main repo documentation and representative frontend/backend files. I\u2019ll pull a little more from the README so the summary covers the declared feature set accurately.\n\n*Viewed file:///Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md*\n\n*Viewed file:///Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md*\n\n### Planner Response\n\n# What This Codebase Does\n\nThis repository is a **monorepo demo/workshop environment for CogHealth EHR**, an Electronic Health Record system.\n\nIt combines:\n\n- **Backend API**: Spring Boot healthcare REST API\n- **Frontend app**: React/TypeScript EHR desktop-style UI\n- **Local infrastructure/data**: Docker services, database schema, and seed data\n- **Workshop exercises**: Intentionally planted HIPAA/compliance gaps and partially implemented modules\n\n## Main Purpose\n\nThe app simulates a healthcare EHR system where users can manage and view:\n\n- **Patients**\n- **Providers**\n- **Encounters/visits**\n- **Vitals**\n- **Clinical notes**\n- **Medications and prescriptions**\n- **Lab orders/results**\n- **Appointments**\n- **Insurance/billing-related data**\n- **Audit logs**\n\nIt is designed for demos, workshops, and compliance/security exercises rather than as a production EHR.\n\n## Repository Layout\n\n```text\nworkshop/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 demos-coghealth-ehr-api/   # Spring Boot REST API\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 demos-coghealth-ehr-web/   # React frontend\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 demos-coghealth-ehr-data/  # Docker infrastructure + seed data\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 start.sh                   # Starts infrastructure, API, and web app\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 stop.sh                    # Stops services\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md\n```\n\n## Backend: `demos-coghealth-ehr-api`\n\nThis is a **Java 11 / Spring Boot 2.7** REST API.\n\nIt provides healthcare data services including:\n\n- **Patient CRUD/search**\n- **Provider lookup**\n- **Encounter management**\n- **Appointment scheduling**\n- **Medication-related services**\n- **Insurance eligibility integration stubs**\n- **FHIR mapping support**\n- **HIPAA-style audit logging**\n\nExample patient API responsibilities include:\n\n- Get patient by ID\n- Get patient by MRN\n- Search patients\n- Create/update patient records\n\nThe backend uses:\n\n- **Spring Data JPA / Hibernate**\n- **PostgreSQL**\n- **Spring Security + JWT**\n- **Redis**\n- **RabbitMQ**\n- **MapStruct**\n- **Lombok**\n- **Spring AOP for audit logging**\n- **SpringDoc OpenAPI / Swagger**\n\n## Frontend: `demos-coghealth-ehr-web`\n\nThis is a **React 19 + TypeScript + Vite** application styled with Tailwind CSS.\n\nIt provides an EHR-like desktop interface with pages for:\n\n- **Dashboard**: `/`\n- **Patient search**: `/patients/search`\n- **Patient chart**: `/patients/:id`\n- **Schedule**: `/schedule`\n- **Medications**: `/medications`\n- **Labs**: `/labs`\n- **Vitals**: `/vitals`\n- **Reports**: `/reports`\n- **Settings**: `/settings`\n\nIt includes UI patterns typical of an EHR:\n\n- Patient banners\n- Search/autocomplete\n- Modals/dialogs\n- Status badges\n- Session timeout handling\n- Audit/logout logging\n- Clinical workflow screens\n\nThe frontend talks to the backend via an API client using:\n\n```ts\nVITE_API_URL || 'http://localhost:8080/api'\n```\n\n## Data/Infrastructure: `demos-coghealth-ehr-data`\n\nThis directory defines local infrastructure with Docker Compose.\n\nServices include:\n\n- **PostgreSQL**: primary clinical database\n- **Redis**: cache/session store\n- **RabbitMQ**: async messaging / HL7-style workflows\n- **Elasticsearch**: audit log/search storage\n- **Kibana**: audit log UI\n- **Keycloak**: SSO/RBAC/MFA demo identity provider\n- **HAPI FHIR**: listed but commented out\n\nThe seed data includes:\n\n- 50+ patients\n- Providers\n- Encounters\n- Clinical data\n- Insurance data\n- Audit log examples\n\n## Compliance Workshop Angle\n\nA key part of this repo is that it contains **intentionally planted HIPAA compliance issues** for audit/demo exercises.\n\nExamples called out in the documentation include:\n\n- Legacy direct JDBC access bypassing audit logging\n- Batch exports without audit logging\n- PHI written to temp files\n- SSN caching concerns\n- Missing access logging on endpoints\n\nSo the codebase is not just an EHR demo; it is also a **training environment for finding and fixing healthcare compliance/security issues**.\n\n## How It Runs\n\nThe intended quick start is:\n\n```bash\n./start.sh\n```\n\nThat starts:\n\n- Docker infrastructure\n- Spring Boot API at `http://localhost:8080/api`\n- React frontend at `http://localhost:3000`\n\nUseful URLs:\n\n- **Web app**: `http://localhost:3000`\n- **Swagger UI**: `http://localhost:8080/api/swagger-ui/index.html`\n- **API health**: `http://localhost:8080/api/actuator/health`\n- **RabbitMQ UI**: `http://localhost:15672`\n- **Kibana**: `http://localhost:5601`\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nThis codebase is a **full-stack demo EHR platform** for healthcare workflow, frontend UI demos, backend API exercises, local infrastructure practice, and HIPAA/security compliance workshops."
  }
}
