[2026-05-14T19:45:04.588394+00:00] post_cascade_response
  Full data: {
  "agent_action_name": "post_cascade_response",
  "trajectory_id": "",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-14T19:45:04.588394+00:00",
  "tool_info": {
    "response": "Need final concise summary with citations. Mention untracked.## Codebase summary\n\nThis repo is a **monorepo workshop/demo environment for CogHealth EHR**, an Electronic Health Record application with a React frontend, Spring Boot backend, and local infrastructure/data setup. The top-level README describes it as a combined frontend/API/data repo for workshops and demos. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"1-5\" />\n\n## Main structure\n\n```text\nworkshop/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 demos-coghealth-ehr-api/   # Spring Boot REST API\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 demos-coghealth-ehr-web/   # React/Vite frontend\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 demos-coghealth-ehr-data/  # Docker infrastructure and seed data\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 start.sh                   # Starts infra + API + web\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 stop.sh                    # Stops services\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md                  # Main setup and architecture docs\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 AGENTS.md                  # Agent/project instructions\n```\n\nThe documented repo layout is in the main README. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"55-65\" />\n\n## Backend: `demos-coghealth-ehr-api`\n\nThe backend is a **Java 11 / Spring Boot 2.7.18 REST API** for healthcare data services. It uses:\n\n- Spring Web\n- Spring Data JPA / Hibernate\n- PostgreSQL\n- Flyway migrations\n- Spring Security with JWT\n- Redis\n- Spring AOP for audit logging\n- MapStruct\n- Lombok\n- SpringDoc OpenAPI / Swagger\n- HAPI HL7/FHIR libraries\n\nThe Maven configuration confirms Java 11 and Spring Boot 2.7.18. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-api/pom.xml\" lines=\"7-28\" />\n\n### Backend domain areas\n\nThe API models a fairly complete EHR domain:\n\n- Patients\n- Providers\n- Encounters\n- Clinical notes\n- Vitals\n- Allergies\n- Diagnoses\n- Medications\n- Lab orders/results\n- Insurance coverage\n- Chronic condition management\n- Auth/users\n- Audit events\n\nThe main Java package is organized into controllers, services, repositories, DTOs, mappers, config, audit, legacy, and domain packages.\n\nImportant backend folders include:\n\n```text\nsrc/main/java/com/medchart/ehr/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 controller/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 service/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 repository/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 domain/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 dto/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 mapper/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 config/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 audit/\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 legacy/\n```\n\nThis is also documented in the README. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"193-216\" />\n\n### Backend APIs\n\nMain controllers include:\n\n- `AuthController` \u2014 login/token/profile\n- `PatientController` \u2014 patient CRUD/search\n- `ProviderController` \u2014 provider operations\n- `EncounterController` \u2014 encounters, vitals, notes\n- `LegacyExportController` \u2014 bulk legacy export\n\nThe README lists these endpoints and responsibilities. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"134-143\" />\n\n### Security and audit\n\nThe backend has JWT authentication and HIPAA-style audit logging using AOP annotations such as:\n\n```java\n@AuditAccess(action = AuditAction.READ, resourceType = \"Patient\", description = \"View patient\")\n```\n\nAudit-related classes live under `audit/`, including `AuditAspect`, `AuditService`, `AuditEvent`, `PatientAccessLogger`, and `MedicationAuditLogger`. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"159-175\" />\n\nThere are also **intentional HIPAA compliance gaps** in the codebase for workshop/audit demo purposes, including unsafe SSN logging, unaudited exports, direct JDBC access, SSN caching, and PHI temp file handling. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"181-191\" />\n\n## Frontend: `demos-coghealth-ehr-web`\n\nThe frontend is a **React + TypeScript + Vite** app styled with Tailwind and using `lucide-react` icons. The package file currently lists React 19, Vite 7, TypeScript, React Router, TanStack Query, Zustand, React Hook Form, Zod, Jest, and Tailwind. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/package.json\" lines=\"6-47\" />\n\nMain frontend structure:\n\n```text\nsrc/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 App.tsx\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pages/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 components/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 services/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 types/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 context/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 hooks/\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 utils/\n```\n\nKey pages include:\n\n- Dashboard\n- Patient search\n- Patient chart\n- Schedule\n- Lab results\n- Vitals\n- Medications\n- Reports\n- Settings\n- Billing\n\nThe main app sets up routing/navigation and an EHR-style desktop UI with patient search, session timer, user controls, and toolbar navigation. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"117-126\" />\n\nThe app defaults to a desktop medical-records aesthetic rather than a consumer/mobile UI. Navigation includes Dashboard, Patients, Schedule, Labs, Vitals, Medications, Reports, and Settings. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"128-219\" />\n\n## Data/infrastructure: `demos-coghealth-ehr-data`\n\nThe data/infrastructure component contains:\n\n- `docker-compose.yml`\n- `seed.sql`\n- `start-infrastructure.sh`\n- Keycloak realm config\n\nIt is used to run local dependencies such as PostgreSQL, Redis, and RabbitMQ. The top-level README says `start.sh` starts:\n\n- PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ via Docker\n- Backend on `http://localhost:8080/api`\n- Frontend on `http://localhost:3000`\n\n<ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"7-23\" />\n\n## Running the app\n\nTop-level quick start:\n\n```bash\n./start.sh\n```\n\nStop everything:\n\n```bash\n./stop.sh\n```\n\n`start.sh` starts Docker services, launches the Spring Boot backend with Java 11 and local DB env vars, then starts the frontend on port 3000. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/start.sh\" lines=\"8-35\" />\n\nManual setup is also documented:\n\n```bash\n# API\ncd demos-coghealth-ehr-api\nmvn spring-boot:run\n\n# Web\ncd demos-coghealth-ehr-web\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nThe main README says required tooling is Java 11, Node 20.19+ or 22.12+, Maven, and Docker Desktop. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"48-54\" />\n\n## Demo users\n\nThe app includes seeded/demo users, all with password `demo123`:\n\n- `dr.anderson` \u2014 Physician\n- `nurse.johnson` \u2014 Nurse\n- `ma.smith` \u2014 Medical Assistant\n- `frontdesk.wilson` \u2014 Front Desk\n- `billing.garcia` \u2014 Billing\n\n<ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/README.md\" lines=\"67-78\" />\n\n## Notable implementation themes\n\n1. **Healthcare/EHR demo app**  \n   The code models real EHR workflows: patient lookup, chart review, encounters, medications, labs, vitals, scheduling, reports, and billing.\n\n2. **Security/audit workshop focus**  \n   HIPAA-style audit logging is partially implemented, and the repo intentionally includes compliance gaps for demo/training scenarios.\n\n3. **Monorepo orchestration**  \n   Top-level scripts coordinate Docker infra, Java API, and React frontend.\n\n4. **Chronic medication module is incomplete/stubbed**  \n   The agent instructions note chronic medication services exist but need implementation: adherence calculation, pharmacy integration, care gaps, notifications, and dashboard endpoints.\n\n5. **Frontend is UI-rich and demo-oriented**  \n   The web app appears designed to look like an EHR desktop system, with compact dense UI patterns, fake/default patient search data in places, and visible clinical workflows.\n\n## Current repo state note\n\nThe repo has several untracked files/directories, including `.windsurf/`, the PDF workshop file, top-level `README.md`, frontend tests/components/pages/hooks/context, and backend test files. So some of what I summarized may include files present in the working tree but not yet committed."
  }
}
