  "tool_info": {
    "response": "Based on my analysis of the existing test infrastructure, I'll create a comprehensive plan to build E2E tests for this repo.\n\n## Current State Assessment\n\n**Existing Testing Infrastructure:**\n- **Frontend**: Jest + Puppeteer E2E tests (auth.test.ts, dashboard.test.ts, e2e.test.ts)\n- **Backend**: JUnit 5 + Spring Boot Test with H2 in-memory database\n- **Infrastructure**: Docker Compose for local services (PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ)\n- **Test Scripts**: `npm test` and `npm run test:e2e`\n\n**Key Gaps Identified:**\n- Tests are not integrated with backend API (many tests skip API-dependent functionality)\n- No CI/CD pipeline configuration\n- Fragile test selectors (XPath, manual waits)\n- No test data management strategy\n- Limited coverage of critical healthcare workflows\n- No performance/load testing\n- No accessibility testing\n\n## Comprehensive E2E Testing Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation & Infrastructure (Week 1-2)\n\n#### 1.1 Test Environment Setup\n- **Create dedicated test configuration**\n  - Add `application-e2e.yml` for backend with test database\n  - Configure test data seeding scripts\n  - Set up test-specific environment variables\n  \n- **Docker Compose for Test Environment**\n  - Create `docker-compose.test.yml` for isolated test infrastructure\n  - Include test database with seeded data\n  - Configure test Redis and RabbitMQ instances\n\n#### 1.2 Test Framework Improvements\n- **Upgrade Puppeteer Configuration**\n  - Add proper test data management\n  - Implement better selector strategies (data-testid attributes)\n  - Add retry logic for flaky network operations\n  \n- **Add Page Object Model (POM)**\n  - Create page objects for major pages (Dashboard, PatientChart, Schedule, etc.)\n  - Abstract common operations (login, navigation, modal handling)\n  - Centralize element selectors\n\n#### 1.3 Test Data Management\n- **Create Test Data Factory**\n  - Implement test data builders for patients, encounters, medications\n  - Add database seeding scripts for consistent test data\n  - Create test data cleanup utilities\n\n### Phase 2: Core Workflow Coverage (Week 3-5)\n\n#### 2.1 Authentication & Authorization\n- **Login Flow Tests**\n  - Valid credentials for different user roles\n  - Invalid credentials handling\n  - Session timeout and auto-logout\n  - Multi-user session handling\n  \n- **Role-Based Access Control**\n  - Physician vs Nurse vs Admin permissions\n  - Unauthorized access attempts\n  - Feature availability by role\n\n#### 2.2 Patient Management Workflows\n- **Patient Search & Selection**\n  - Search by name, MRN, DOB\n  - Advanced filtering\n  - Patient selection and chart navigation\n  \n- **Patient Chart Operations**\n  - Demographics viewing/editing\n  - Clinical notes creation\n  - Allergy management\n  - Problem list management\n\n#### 2.3 Clinical Documentation\n- **Encounter Management**\n  - New encounter creation\n  - Vitals recording\n  - Clinical note signing\n  - Encounter completion\n  \n- **Orders & Results**\n  - Lab order placement\n  - Medication prescribing\n  - Result review and acknowledgment\n  - Critical result alert handling\n\n#### 2.4 Medication Management\n- **Prescription Workflow**\n  - New prescription creation\n  - Drug interaction checking\n  - Refill management\n  - Pharmacy integration simulation\n\n#### 2.5 Scheduling & Workflow\n- **Appointment Management**\n  - New appointment scheduling\n  - Check-in/check-out flows\n  - Room assignment\n  - Cancellation and rescheduling\n\n### Phase 3: Advanced Testing Scenarios (Week 6-7)\n\n#### 3.1 HIPAA Compliance Testing\n- **Audit Logging Verification**\n  - Verify audit events for all PHI access\n  - Test audit log completeness\n  - Validate audit event timestamps and user attribution\n  \n- **Data Privacy**\n  - Verify SSN masking in UI\n  - Test PHI handling in logs\n  - Validate secure session handling\n\n#### 3.2 Integration Testing\n- **API Integration Tests**\n  - Frontend-backend API contract testing\n  - Error handling and retry logic\n  - Offline mode handling\n  \n- **External Service Integration**\n  - Insurance eligibility checks\n  - Pharmacy integration (mocked)\n  - Notification system testing\n\n#### 3.3 Cross-Browser Testing\n- **Browser Compatibility**\n  - Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\n  - Mobile responsive testing\n  - Accessibility testing with screen readers\n\n### Phase 4: Test Automation & CI/CD (Week 8)\n\n#### 4.1 CI/CD Pipeline Integration\n- **GitHub Actions Workflow**\n  - Automated test execution on PR\n  - Parallel test execution\n  - Test result reporting and artifacts\n  \n- **Docker Integration**\n  - Containerized test execution\n  - Environment parity\n  - Cleanup and resource management\n\n#### 4.2 Test Reporting & Monitoring\n- **Test Reports**\n  - HTML test reports with screenshots\n  - Video recordings for failed tests\n  - Performance metrics collection\n  \n- **Test Metrics Dashboard**\n  - Test pass/fail trends\n  - Flaky test identification\n  - Coverage tracking\n\n### Phase 5: Specialized Testing (Week 9-10)\n\n#### 5.1 Performance Testing\n- **Load Testing**\n  - Concurrent user simulation\n  - API response time monitoring\n  - Database query performance\n  \n- **Stress Testing**\n  - Peak load scenarios\n  - Memory leak detection\n  - Resource exhaustion handling\n\n#### 5.2 Security Testing\n- **OWASP Top 10 Coverage**\n  - SQL injection prevention\n  - XSS vulnerability testing\n  - CSRF protection verification\n  \n- **Authentication Security**\n  - Session fixation prevention\n  - Password strength enforcement\n  - Brute force protection\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n#### File Structure\n```\ndemos-coghealth-ehr-web/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 e2e/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 pages/              # Page Object Models\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 DashboardPage.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 PatientChartPage.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 SchedulePage.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 LoginPage.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 fixtures/           # Test data\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 patients.json\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 encounters.json\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 medications.json\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 helpers/            # Test utilities\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 apiHelpers.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 dbHelpers.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 authHelpers.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 workflows/          # Workflow tests\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 patient-workflow.test.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 prescribing-workflow.test.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 scheduling-workflow.test.ts\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 integration/        # Integration tests\n\u2502   \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api-integration.test.ts\n\u2502   \u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 hipaa-compliance.test.ts\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 auth.test.ts            # Existing - enhance\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 dashboard.test.ts       # Existing - enhance\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 e2e.test.ts             # Existing - refactor\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 docker-compose.test.yml     # Test infrastructure\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 jest.config.e2e.cjs         # E2E-specific config\n```\n\n#### Key Dependencies to Add\n```json\n{\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.40.0\",  // Consider migrating from Puppeteer\n    \"test-data-bot\": \"^0.9.0\",      // Test data generation\n    \"mongodb-memory-server\": \"^9.0.0\" // If using MongoDB for test data\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Configuration Updates\n- Update `jest.config.cjs` to support E2E-specific configuration\n- Add environment variable management for test environments\n- Create test-specific startup scripts\n\n### Success Criteria\n\n1. **Coverage**: 80%+ of critical user journeys covered\n2. **Reliability**: <5% flaky test rate\n3. **Execution Time**: Full E2E suite <30 minutes\n4. **Maintenance**: Easy to update when UI changes\n5. **Integration**: Seamless CI/CD integration\n6. **Reporting**: Clear, actionable test failure reports\n\n### Risk Mitigation\n\n1. **Flaky Tests**: Implement retry logic, better waits, and stable selectors\n2. **Test Data Management**: Use transaction rollback and isolated test databases\n3. **Environment Parity**: Containerized test environments matching production\n4. **Maintenance Overhead**: Page Object Model and reusable test components\n5. **Slow Execution**: Parallel test execution and smart test selection\n\nThis plan provides a structured approach to building comprehensive E2E tests while maintaining the existing EHR desktop aesthetic and ensuring HIPAA compliance validation."
