    "response": "Based on my exploration of the codebase, I can see that dark mode infrastructure already exists but isn't fully implemented. Here's my plan to complete the dark mode implementation:\n\n## Current State\n- \u2705 `ThemeContext.tsx` exists with full theme switching logic (light/dark/system)\n- \u2705 `ThemeToggle.tsx` component exists but isn't integrated\n- \u274c `ThemeProvider` is not wrapped around the app in `main.tsx`\n- \u274c All CSS styles in `index.css` are hardcoded light-mode colors\n- \u274c Components use EHR-specific classes that don't respond to theme changes\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n### 1. Integrate ThemeProvider\n- Wrap the App component with `ThemeProvider` in `main.tsx`\n- This will enable the theme context throughout the application\n\n### 2. Add Theme Toggle to UI\n- Integrate the existing `ThemeToggle` component into the header\n- Place it in the header's right section alongside user info and logout\n- Ensure it's visible and accessible\n\n### 3. Update CSS for Dark Mode Support\n- Convert hardcoded EHR styles to use CSS custom properties (CSS variables)\n- Create dark mode variants using `data-theme=\"dark\"` selector\n- Key styles to update:\n  - Background colors (body, panels, headers)\n  - Text colors (primary, secondary, muted)\n  - Border colors\n  - Button styles and hover states\n  - Table styles\n  - Input field styles\n  - Alert/notification colors\n\n### 4. Update Component Styles\n- Review and update components that use inline styles or hardcoded colors\n- Ensure Tailwind classes work with dark mode (using `dark:` prefix where needed)\n- Focus on commonly used components: Button, Card, Input, Modal\n\n### 5. Test and Verify\n- Test theme switching between light/dark/system modes\n- Verify all pages display correctly in both themes\n- Check that system preference detection works\n- Run `npm run build` to ensure no build errors\n\n### 6. Refine Colors\n- Ensure dark mode colors maintain good contrast and readability\n- Preserve the EHR desktop aesthetic while making it work in dark mode\n- Test on different pages (Dashboard, Patient Search, Settings, etc.)\n\nWould you like me to proceed with this implementation plan?"
