    "response": "*Rules used for this response:*\n- (Always On) Triggered Rule: AGENTS.md\n\n### Planner Response\n\nI\u2019ll inspect `DashboardPage.tsx` around the inbox mapping helpers to trace exactly how generic patient records become typed inbox items.\n\n*Found code context*\n\n### Planner Response\n\n# How Inbox Type Is Determined\n\nThe dashboard does **not** derive the inbox item type from real clinical data on the `Patient` object.\n\nInstead, `mapPatientToInbox` assigns a simulated type based purely on the patient\u2019s array index:\n\n```ts\nconst types: InboxItem['type'][] = ['lab', 'imaging', 'message', 'refill', 'order', 'cosign'];\n\ntype: types[index % types.length],\n```\n\nSo the mapping cycles through the fixed list:\n\n- **Index 0**: `lab`\n- **Index 1**: `imaging`\n- **Index 2**: `message`\n- **Index 3**: `refill`\n- **Index 4**: `order`\n- **Index 5**: `cosign`\n- **Index 6**: `lab` again\n- **Index 7**: `imaging` again\n\nThe title is generated from the same index-based type:\n\n```ts\ntitle: `${types[index % types.length].toUpperCase()} Result`,\n```\n\n# Source of the Generic Data\n\nThe dashboard fetches generic patients here:\n\n```ts\nconst result = await patientService.search('', 0, 20);\nconst patients = result.content;\nsetInboxItems(patients.slice(0, 10).map((p, i) => mapPatientToInbox(p, i)));\n```\n\nThe `Patient` type only includes demographics/identity fields like name, MRN, DOB, gender, contact info, etc. It does **not** include inbox-specific fields like lab results, imaging orders, messages, or refills.\n\n# Summary\n\nThe inbox types are **demo/synthetic data**, assigned deterministically by list position, not by patient attributes or backend clinical records."
  }
}
