[2026-05-20T00:24:19.508085+00:00] post_cascade_response
  Full data: {
  "agent_action_name": "post_cascade_response",
  "trajectory_id": "",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-20T00:24:19.508085+00:00",
  "tool_info": {
    "response": "Based on my exploration of the `demos-coghealth-ehr-web` frontend, here's a comprehensive overview of the routing and component patterns:\n\n## **Routing Structure**\n\n**Technology**: React Router v7 with `BrowserRouter`, `Routes`, and `Route` components\n\n**Main Routes** (defined in <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"1-50\" />):\n- `/` - DashboardPage\n- `/patients` - PatientSearchPage  \n- `/patients/:id` - PatientChartPage (dynamic patient ID)\n- `/schedule` - SchedulePage\n- `/labs` - LabResultsPage\n- `/vitals` - VitalsPage\n- `/medications` - MedicationsPage\n- `/reports` - ReportsPage\n- `/settings` - SettingsPage\n\n**Navigation Pattern**: \n- Global navigation header with toolbar buttons\n- Active state detection for nested routes (e.g., `/patients/:id` activates `/patients` nav item)\n- Global patient search in header that navigates to patient charts\n\n## **Component Architecture**\n\n### **Page Components** (`src/pages/`)\n- **Functional components** using React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`)\n- **Router hooks**: `useNavigate`, `useLocation`, `useParams` for navigation\n- **Service integration**: All pages use service layer for API calls\n- **Modal/dialog patterns**: Consistent use of AlertDialog, PrintDialog, PrescriptionDialog, OrderDialog\n\n### **UI Components** (`src/components/ui/`)\n**Reusable component library** with EHR-specific styling:\n- **Button** - Variants: primary, secondary, danger, ghost; sizes: sm, md, lg\n- **Card** - Padding variants: none, sm, md, lg; with CardHeader subcomponent\n- **Input** - Standardized input styling\n- **Modal** - AlertDialog, ConfirmDialog for interactions\n- **Badge, StatusBadge, FlagChip** - Status indicators\n- **LoadingOverlay, Tooltip** - UX enhancements\n\n### **Domain Components** (`src/components/`)\n**Patient-specific components**:\n- **PatientBanner** - Patient header with demographics, alerts, allergies\n- **PatientSearch** - Search functionality with results display\n\n### **Service Layer** (`src/services/`)\n**API abstraction pattern**:\n- **api.ts** - Base fetch wrapper with error handling and query params\n- **patientService.ts** - Patient-specific API methods (getById, search, create, update)\n- **auditService.ts** - Audit logging for patient access\n\n### **Type System** (`src/types/`)\n**TypeScript interfaces** for domain entities:\n- **Patient** - Comprehensive patient data model\n- **Address, PatientIdentifier, EmergencyContact** - Sub-types\n- **Medication, Encounter, Lab, Vitals** - Clinical data types\n- **Enums** - Gender, MaritalStatus, IdentifierType, etc.\n\n## **Styling Patterns**\n\n### **EHR Desktop Aesthetic**\nThe app uses a **classic Windows/desktop EHR style** with custom CSS classes:\n\n**Key styling patterns** (from <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/index.css\" lines=\"43-238\" />):\n- **`.ehr-panel`** - Gray panels with inset shadows\n- **`.ehr-button`** - Gradient buttons with 3D bevel effects\n- **`.ehr-toolbar`** - Gradient toolbar backgrounds\n- **`.ehr-tab`** - Tab styling with active states\n- **`.ehr-header`** - Blue gradient headers\n- **`.ehr-input`** - Standardized input fields with focus states\n\n### **Tailwind Integration**\n- Custom color palette (primary blues, secondary grays)\n- Small font sizes (10-11px) typical of EHR applications\n- Gradient backgrounds for headers and buttons\n- Inset shadows for 3D desktop effects\n\n## **Key Patterns**\n\n### **Data Flow**\n1. **Service layer** handles API calls\n2. **Pages** fetch data via services in `useEffect`\n3. **Local state** manages UI state (filters, modals, expanded panels)\n4. **Navigation** uses React Router for route changes\n\n### **State Management**\n- **Local component state** with `useState`\n- **No global state management** (no Redux/Zustand for UI state)\n- **Services** handle data fetching and caching\n\n### **Component Patterns**\n- **Compact, functional components** \n- **Lucide React icons** throughout\n- **Consistent modal/dialog patterns**\n- **Expandable panels** with toggle functionality\n- **Tab-based navigation** within pages\n- **Alert/notification system** for user feedback\n\n### **EHR-Specific Features**\n- **Session timeout management** with activity tracking\n- **Audit logging** for patient access\n- **Global patient search** with autocomplete\n- **Clinical decision support** alerts\n- **Print/prescription/order dialogs**\n\nThis architecture follows a **traditional EHR desktop application pattern** with modern React patterns, maintaining the familiar clinical workflow while using contemporary web technologies."
  }
}
