[2026-05-20T00:27:36.393232+00:00] post_cascade_response
  Full data: {
  "agent_action_name": "post_cascade_response",
  "trajectory_id": "",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-20T00:27:36.393232+00:00",
  "tool_info": {
    "response": "Explored `demos-coghealth-ehr-web`; it\u2019s a compact Vite/React EHR desktop-style app.\n\n**Structure**\n- Entrypoint is `src/main.tsx`, which mounts `<App />` under `StrictMode`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/main.tsx\" />\n- Main shell, navigation, session dialogs, route table, and status bar all live in `src/App.tsx`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" />\n- Feature pages are flat under `src/pages`: dashboard, patient search/chart, schedule, labs, vitals, medications, reports, settings, plus an unused-looking `BillingPage.tsx`.\n- Shared components are split into `components/ui` and `components/patient`.\n- Services and typed API models live in `src/services` and `src/types`.\n\n**Routing**\n- Uses `react-router-dom` with `BrowserRouter`, `Routes`, `Route`, `Link`, `useNavigate`, and `useLocation`.\n- Route definitions are centralized in `App.tsx`: `/`, `/patients`, `/patients/:id`, `/schedule`, `/labs`, `/vitals`, `/medications`, `/reports`, `/settings`. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"282-301\" />\n- Navigation items are also defined in `App.tsx`; active state compares `location.pathname`, with special handling for `/patients/:id`. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"117-126\" />\n- Patient chart reads route params via `useParams()` and loads the patient by ID. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/pages/PatientChartPage.tsx\" lines=\"59-101\" />\n\n**Component Patterns**\n- Styling is a hybrid of Tailwind utility classes plus custom global EHR classes in `src/index.css`; the visual language is Windows XP / legacy clinical desktop: tiny fonts, gradients, beveled panels, toolbars, tabs, dense tables. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/index.css\" lines=\"43-88\" />\n- UI primitives are intentionally thin wrappers over these global classes, e.g. `Card` wraps `ehr-panel`, `Button` wraps `ehr-button`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/components/ui/Card.tsx\" /> <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/components/ui/Button.tsx\" />\n- Pages are mostly self-contained functional components with local `useState`, `useEffect`, and `useMemo` state rather than global stores.\n- Icons consistently come from `lucide-react`.\n- API access goes through a small typed `fetch` wrapper using `VITE_API_URL` with localhost fallback. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/services/api.ts\" />\n\n**Notable Pattern**\n- Pages often fetch backend patient data, then map it into demo-specific UI models locally; `DashboardPage` is a good example. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/pages/DashboardPage.tsx\" lines=\"144-181\" />\n- For frontend changes, the safest path is to preserve the existing dense EHR desktop style, reuse `ehr-*` classes and compact Tailwind utilities, and validate with `npm run build` from `demos-coghealth-ehr-web`."
  }
}
