  "timestamp": "2026-05-20T00:28:40.747934+00:00",
  "tool_info": {
    "response": "Explored the frontend structure in `demos-coghealth-ehr-web`.\n\n**Architecture**\n- Vite + React 19 + TypeScript app, with scripts in <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/package.json\" />.\n- Entry point is minimal: `main.tsx` imports global CSS and renders `App` inside `StrictMode`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/main.tsx\" />\n- Main app shell, navigation, session timeout handling, global patient search, footer/status bar, and route declarations all live in `App.tsx`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" />\n\n**Routing**\n- Uses `react-router-dom` with `BrowserRouter`, `Routes`, and `Route`; routing is centralized in `App.tsx`. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"281-300\" />\n- Current routes:\n  - `/` \u2192 `DashboardPage`\n  - `/patients` \u2192 `PatientSearchPage`\n  - `/patients/:id` \u2192 `PatientChartPage`\n  - `/schedule` \u2192 `SchedulePage`\n  - `/labs` \u2192 `LabResultsPage`\n  - `/vitals` \u2192 `VitalsPage`\n  - `/medications` \u2192 `MedicationsPage`\n  - `/reports` \u2192 `ReportsPage`\n  - `/settings` \u2192 `SettingsPage`\n- There is also a `BillingPage.tsx`, but it is not currently wired into `App.tsx`.\n\n**Navigation Patterns**\n- Desktop/mobile navigation is embedded in the `Navigation` component inside `App.tsx`.\n- Nav items are declared as an array with path/icon/label, using `lucide-react` icons. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"117-126\" />\n- Active state checks exact path matches, plus `/patients/*` for the patient nav item. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.tsx\" lines=\"198-207\" />\n- Page-to-page navigation usually uses `useNavigate`, especially for patient chart jumps from search/dashboard/schedule/medications.\n\n**Component Organization**\n- Pages are flat under `src/pages`.\n- Reusable UI components are under `src/components/ui`, with partial barrel exports in `src/components/ui/index.ts`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/components/ui/index.ts\" />\n- Patient-specific components live under `src/components/patient`, including `PatientBanner` and `PatientSearch`.\n- Shared service/API logic lives under `src/services`; typed domain models live under `src/types`.\n\n**Styling Patterns**\n- Styling is a mix of Tailwind utility classes plus global EHR-style CSS classes in `index.css`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/index.css\" />\n- Visual language is intentionally desktop/EHR/Windows-XP-like: small `11px` typography, gray panels, beveled buttons, gradient title bars, dense tables.\n- Key reusable classes include `ehr-panel`, `ehr-button`, `ehr-button-primary`, `ehr-input`, `ehr-header`, `ehr-subheader`, `ehr-toolbar`, `ehr-tab`, and alert/grid classes. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/index.css\" lines=\"43-88\" />\n- `App.css` appears to be leftover Vite starter CSS and is not imported by the current app entry. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/App.css\" />\n\n**Data/API Patterns**\n- API base URL defaults to `http://localhost:8080/api`, overrideable with `VITE_API_URL`. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/services/api.ts\" lines=\"1-11\" />\n- Services wrap typed `api.get/post/put/delete` calls, e.g. `patientService.search`, `getById`, `create`, `update`. <ref_file file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/services/patientService.ts\" />\n- Several pages combine API-backed patient data with local/demo default data for chart sections, labs, meds, vitals, etc. <ref_snippet file=\"/Users/wesconvery/dev/cog-gtm/workshop/demos-coghealth-ehr-web/src/pages/PatientChartPage.tsx\" lines=\"39-56\" />\n\n**Implementation Conventions**\n- Pages are large, self-contained React function components with local `useState` / `useEffect` state.\n- UI actions commonly open modal dialogs or `AlertDialog`s rather than route elsewhere.\n- `lucide-react` is the standard icon source.\n- Existing design system is compact and dense; future frontend changes should preserve the EHR desktop style and reuse `ehr-*` classes/components rather than introducing a new visual language."
  }
}
